  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Front Desk Binder",
    "overview": "Every well-run community keeps a binder at the front desk: a green tab for each section, a white page under each tab, this week's calendar and today's menu on top. This system is that binder rendered as a national-operator website. The ground is a warm off-white; each module opens with a forest green header bar carrying the section title on the left and a single \"see all\" link on the right, joined to a white panel beneath. A small apricot square sits before every bar title, and the same apricot is the one action colour on the site: \"Book a visit\", and the marker on today's calendar day. Brick red exists for the site-wide alert band, urgent notices and inspection citations only. Nothing about the surface is meant to surprise; the argument is carried by what the panels hold: dated, timed, roomed, priced and cited information set at sizes a 78-year-old can read on a phone.\n\nDensity is moderate and even. Content sits in bordered paper panels on a single 1180px column, sections stack at a 34px gap, and 17px is the smallest running text anywhere. The page is flat: depth is drawn with 1px warm rules and the forest-on-off-white contrast, never with shadows on content. Headings are Bricolage Grotesque, a warm grotesque with enough personality to name a place; everything that has to be read is Atkinson Hyperlegible Next. Motion is short (180 to 250ms) on one spring-like ease and switches off under reduced motion.\n\nOne further world lives inside this one: the violet \"module structure\" overlay. It is driven by a fixed demo pill that sits outside the site chrome. When it is on, every section grows a dashed violet label naming the module, its editor, its content type and its publishing lane, and each section bar is ringed in violet. With the pill off, no violet appears anywhere on the site.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Warm off-white ground, forest green fields and section bars, apricot for the single action, brick red only for alerts and citations",
      "Bricolage Grotesque headings over Atkinson Hyperlegible Next text; 18px body, 17px floor",
      "Every home module is a forest bar joined to a paper panel: title left, one link right, apricot square before the title",
      "Flat surfaces with 1px warm rules; the shadow token belongs to the floating demo pill, not to content",
      "Pill buttons at 48px minimum, 10px panel corners, 6px small corners",
      "Violet is the annotation layer for structure mode only, switched from a fixed demo pill"
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Apricot Rule",
        "body": "Apricot fills the primary action and marks \"today\"; the only other places it appears are the 10px square before a bar title and the nav hover underline. Every other button is forest, outline or paper.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Red Means Act Rule",
        "body": "Brick red appears only on the alert band, urgent notices, citations and cancellations, things a family must react to. It is never used for emphasis, headings or decoration.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Violet Overlay Rule",
        "body": "Violet belongs to the demo pill and the structure-mode annotation layer. With structure off, no violet is visible anywhere on the site.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Words Beside Colour Rule",
        "body": "Every colour that carries state (green dot, category square, citation red, lane chip) sits beside text that says the same thing. Nothing is conveyed by colour alone.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The 17px Floor Rule",
        "body": "No running text, cell, caption, hint or key on the site is smaller than 17px; body copy is 18px. Fine print is expressed by colour (`ink-2`), never by size.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Grotesque Names, Hyperlegible Reads Rule",
        "body": "Bricolage Grotesque is for names, headings, day and meal names and numerals. Any run of text longer than a line, and the alert band's own heading (20px, tracking reset to 0), is Atkinson.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Square Before The Title Rule",
        "body": "Every section bar title carries a 10px apricot square (2px corners, 12px gap) before it. It is the bar's mark; it is never added to headings outside a bar.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Bar Then Panel Rule",
        "body": "Every home module is a forest bar with the title left and exactly one \"see all\" link right, joined to a paper panel. The bar is the section separator; there are no rules between modules.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Column Rule",
        "body": "All content shares the 1180px column. Full-bleed colour (alert, header, identity, page header, banner, footer) is applied to the band, never to the wrap.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Border Not Shadow Rule",
        "body": "A panel, card or tile gets a 1px `rule` border and no shadow, on either paper. The float shadow belongs to elements fixed over the page, never to content in the flow.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ring Not Fill Rule",
        "body": "Structure mode annotates by ringing (inset 2px `violet-line` on bars) and labelling (dashed labels), never by recolouring the site's own surfaces.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep every running text size at 17px or above and body copy at 18px / 1.55; express \"fine print\" with `ink-2`, not a smaller size.",
      "Do give every interactive element a 44px minimum hit area (48px for buttons and fields, 46px for tabs, 50px for nav links) and the 3px `forest` focus outline at 3px offset.",
      "Do pair every status colour with words: a green dot with \"Updated today\", a red row with \"1 citation\", a category square with a visually hidden label.",
      "Do open every home module with a forest bar (title left with the apricot square, one link right) joined to a paper panel, and close the panel with a stamp or one sentence in `ink-2`.",
      "Do use one apricot button per view for the primary action; make every other button forest, outline or paper.",
      "Do put semantic tables (`caption`, `th scope`) inside a horizontally scrolling card rather than letting the page side-scroll.",
      "Do use the inline SVG icon set (24px viewBox, 2px stroke, round caps) at 1.15em beside text; sized 26 to 28px only in the alert band and document rows.",
      "Do keep the demo pill and every violet element outside the site's own chrome, so the site reads as real with structure off."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use brick red for anything other than the alert band, urgent notices, citations and cancellations.",
      "Don't let violet appear outside the demo pill and structure mode; it is the annotation layer, not a brand colour.",
      "Don't set white text on apricot; apricot always carries `ink`.",
      "Don't put a shadow on a panel, card or tile; the float shadow is for the fixed demo pill only.",
      "Don't set running text in Bricolage Grotesque; the grotesque is for names, headings, day and meal names and numerals only.",
      "Don't use uppercase labels as kickers above headings; the Label style is reserved for the key half of a key/value pair.",
      "Don't add a second link or a button to a section bar; the bar carries the title and exactly one \"see all\" link.",
      "Don't add motion longer than 250ms outside the module-label reveal, and never without a `prefers-reduced-motion` fallback."
    ]
  }
}
